Ye Olde Programme.

Julius Caesar, The Orator.
Puck, Verbal Vitiate.

		Act I: A Dazzling Battle of Wits.
		
		Scene I: A Confusing Verbal Joust.

[Enter Julius Caesar and Puck]

Puck: Listen to thy heart! Thou art the product of thyself and a smooth chihuahua! Thou art the difference between thyself and a mighty proud delicious horse. Thou art the sum of thyself and a misused fat-kidneyed beggar. Thou art the sum of thyself and a coward.

Julius Caesar: Thou art the product of a toad and a damned hairy infected foul rotten smelly oozing codpiece. Thou art the sum of thyself and an oozing fatherless snotty vile hog.

Puck: Speak thy mind!

Julius Caesar: Speak thy mind!

Puck: Thou art a toad! Thou art the product of a dusty horrid half-witted villainous lying hairy hairy goat and a toad! Thou art the difference between thyself and a warm healthy honest trustworthy cousin. Thou art the sum of thyself and a vile distasteful leech.

Puck: Speak thy mind!

[Exeunt]







